{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918358-malkavia","id":918358,"title":"Malkavia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-20T18:37:46-07:00","id":918358,"title":"Malkavia","content":"I wish that they would create a supplement to do something more with this. I've been thinking about it. I don't want a clan, covenant, or bloodline. I think it'd be really cool to make it a disease that can strike any vampire. Humans could be carriers, but it should require something that maybe vampires haven't figured out, and certainly can't detect. Like it requires that the human has somehow come into contact with an infected vampires vitae, or maybe just been fed off by an infected vampire. Maybe some vampires are naturally immune, or more likely resistant (so feeding of an infected human isn't an automatic fail, you have to roll). It should either give the vampire access to new and exciting powers, maybe devotions, or warp there existing ones (e.g Daeva cause bipolar, instead of lustly oxytocin). Maybe it even has an aura about infected vamps, you come to speak to the mad gangrel, your senses heighten and you growl at him, are you losing it too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 06-20-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T18:58:15-07:00","id":918361,"title":"","content":"What you're describing is in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55241/Lords-Over-the-Damned-Ventrue\" target=\"_blank\">Ventrue clanbook</a>.<br /> <br /> 'Malkavia is wholly unnatural. It is neither a mental nor physical disease, exactly. It is a mystical affliction, like a magic curse, but it is also transmissable through the blood, like an illness.'<br /> <br /> It also gives them access to the Dementation Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T21:38:39-07:00","id":918433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918358-malkavia?p=918361#post918361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing is in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55241/Lords-Over-the-Damned-Ventrue\" target=\"_blank\">Ventrue clanbook</a>.<br /> <br /> 'Malkavia is wholly unnatural. It is neither a mental nor physical disease, exactly. It is a mystical affliction, like a magic curse, but it is also transmissable through the blood, like an illness.'<br /> <br /> It also gives them access to the Dementation Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> had no idea about that. Derangements were a thing in 1st edition right? does anyone have a suggestion as how best to replace them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T21:56:16-07:00","id":918440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918358-malkavia?p=918433#post918433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">had no idea about that. Derangements were a thing in 1st edition right? does anyone have a suggestion as how best to replace them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Derangements and Flaws have been replaced by Persistent Conditions in second edition. The concept is the same, a hindrance that you can get Beats from by playing up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:18:52-07:00","id":918872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/918358-malkavia?p=918433#post918433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">had no idea about that. Derangements were a thing in 1st edition right? does anyone have a suggestion as how best to replace them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did an update to the disease a ways back, you could use that or modify it to suit your needs. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hNssb3w0QxV6sTEs66qpd1uN49o3L7GS7Hh7zL2os58/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link</a>. Since you're not really interested in Malkavia as a bloodline, I would recommend either removing the bloodline, or making the Gifts accessible to anyone who becomes permanently afflicted, with permanent affliction not counting as a bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T02:41:27-07:00","id":919609,"title":"","content":"Really recommend checking out Clanbook Ventrue if you're interested in Malkavia. They explore the condition in great detail and have some other really great story seeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}